80
00:07:48,610 --> 00:07:52,670
So now, instead, we have
the following theorem.

81
00:07:52,670 --> 00:07:57,150
So we have this interval,
and we have a sequence fn,

82
00:07:57,150 --> 00:08:02,030
and we have f all
defined on this interval.

83
00:08:02,030 --> 00:08:17,430
And if we assume that all of
these fn's are continuous,

84
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:22,230
and b, we assume that
the convergence here,

85
00:08:22,230 --> 00:08:29,230
the convergence of
fn to f is uniform,

86
00:08:29,230 --> 00:08:37,850
then the claim is that then
f here is also continuous.

87
00:08:44,430 --> 00:08:45,330
OK.

88
00:08:45,330 --> 00:08:46,730
So let's try to prove that.

89
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:53,020
So pointwise convergence
is not enough to guarantee

90
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:55,300
