197
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:53,060
equal to 0 to infinity of x to
the power k over k factorial.

198
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:55,480
This convergence
here is uniform.

199
00:17:55,480 --> 00:18:02,100
It's uniform assuming that you
do it on a compact interval.

200
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:18,820
So it's uniform on any
fixed interval of the form,

201
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:24,600
say, minus L to L.

202
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:27,120
So if you're fixing
an interval like this,

203
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:30,320
then the convergence is uniform.

204
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:36,160
And so this means that since
these guys here are continuous,

205
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:40,380
then it implies that this
one here is also continuous.

206
00:18:47,088 --> 00:18:50,610
So this is implied by the
theorem that we just proved.

207
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:59,760
So now this will--

208
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:02,480
uniform convergence.

209
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:08,160
There's another way of thinking
about uniform convergence that,

210
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:13,490
in a way, makes it more natural.

211
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:21,120
So remember that
if we looked at--

212
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:22,920
so if we take an
interval-- let's

213
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:28,440
say that this is an interval
from a to b. a and b

214
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:31,200
are real numbers.

215
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:35,750
Then we looked at the space
of continuous functions

216
00:19:35,750 --> 00:19:38,750
on this interval.

217
00:19:38,750 --> 00:19:41,570
And this space had
a natural metric.

218
00:19:41,570 --> 00:19:45,950
So I'm using here that both
endpoints are included.

219
00:19:45,950 --> 00:19:50,380
This space here has
a natural metric.

220
00:19:56,830 --> 00:20:02,270
And that metric is that if
you take two functions--

221
00:20:02,270 --> 00:20:06,070
two continuous functions--
on the interval, then

222
00:20:06,070 --> 00:20:09,310
the distance between
these two functions

223
00:20:09,310 --> 00:20:21,270
is just the max of the
difference between the two

224
00:20:21,270 --> 00:20:22,090
functions.

225
00:20:30,510 --> 00:20:33,780
The difference--
again, why is this?

226
00:20:33,780 --> 00:20:35,900
The difference is continuous.

227
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:39,620
So this means that
the maximum is--

228
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:41,040
the difference is continuous.

229
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,660
So this is a
continuous function,

230
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:45,740
and it's still continuous
if you take absolute value.

231
00:20:45,740 --> 00:20:49,060
And so this means that the
maximum by the extreme value

232
00:20:49,060 --> 00:20:50,105
theorem is achieved.

233
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:57,340
And so this here was a
natural distance between them.

234
00:20:57,340 --> 00:21:02,300
Now to say that
the sequence here--

235
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:08,500
to say that the sequence
fn is converging uniformly,

236
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:12,340
you can think about that
in terms of this distance.

237
00:21:12,340 --> 00:21:16,080
So we have the
following proposition.

238
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:30,060
fn converge uniformly
to f if and only

239
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:53,210
